From d579cdd1a769dba05769b287774d7f4565c6744b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Krishna (via Claude)" <krishhs89@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 11:54:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Make text embedding, fine-tuning, and verification training
 disconnect-safe

Completes the Colab-resumability work: captioning and image embedding were
already checkpointed (4cacf67, bd7af0d, 27e14e7); this covers the remaining
long-running steps:

- embed_text: per-batch JSONL checkpoint (same pattern as embed_image);
  monolithic encode() replaced with batched+fsync'd loop; Chroma still
  rebuilt once from the merged set on completion
- finetune_text: one-epoch-at-a-time training with atomic
  _finetune_state.json; resume loads last saved weights; warmup only on
  fresh runs; distrusts state without a loadable saved model
- train_verification: pair-image CLIP embeddings cached per batch to
  _clip_embed_cache.jsonl (the slow step; MLP training itself is seconds)
- build_pairs needed no change: its slow step (second-view downloads)
  already skips existing files
- notebook: per-stage notes on how to resume after a disconnect

Validated: 20/20 checkpoint-logic tests pass (12 new, 8 existing as
regression). Full-suite + real-pipeline validation to run on local GPU / CI
(sandbox couldn't install torch).
